; The ONE variable: `layout_direction` on a CHILD of a right-to-left Control —
; absent (INHERITED) on one bar, `2` (LTR) on the other. `Control::is_layout_rtl`
; climbs to the nearest ancestor Control for INHERITED (control.cpp:3584-3593)
; while an explicit LTR answers from the value alone (control.cpp:3619), so the
; first bar is mirrored inside its parent by `Control::_size_changed`
; (control.cpp:1785-1787) and the second is not. Both bars are FREE children,
; not container children: a container owns its children's rects, so it hides the
; per-child mirror that this scene is here to show. The parent is the same
; offset and width in both rows, and the bars are identical apart from the one
; property, so a mirror that fired on the wrong one is a visible swap.

